Make sure llvm-strip binary is available on Ubuntu

From: Shung-Hsi Yu <shung-hsi.yu@suse.com>

On aarch64 the llvm package wasn't pulled with llvm.sh, and thus
llvm-strip binary was not available. Explicitly install it in
install_clang.sh.

Signed-off-by: Shung-Hsi Yu <shung-hsi.yu@suse.com>
---
 setup-build-env/install_clang.sh |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/setup-build-env/install_clang.sh b/setup-build-env/install_clang.sh
index 59e3aba..1bf28ef 100755
--- a/setup-build-env/install_clang.sh
+++ b/setup-build-env/install_clang.sh
@@ -16,6 +16,10 @@ if [[ "${ID}" == "ubuntu" ]]; then
     curl -O https://apt.llvm.org/llvm.sh
     chmod +x llvm.sh
     sudo ./llvm.sh ${LLVM_VERSION} all
+    # On aarch64 the llvm package wasn't pulled with llvm.sh, and thus
+    # llvm-strip binary was not available. Make sure it is installed.
+    sudo -E apt-get install --no-install-recommends -y \
+        llvm-${LLVM_VERSION}
 elif [[ "${ID}" == "debian" ]]; then
     # For Debian, install packages directly from repos
     # Recent debian considers SHA1 insecure, and llvm.sh hasn't been fixed yet
